Z||000002||Tonker||09-26-2001||11:01 PM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B>What'd you think?  I thought it was OK... <I>could've done without the Vulcan Seven-of-9 rip-off</I>, but maybe that's just me.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Otherwise it seemed ok.  Bakula was better than I expected and the ship looks cool.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>BLASPHEMER!!!</B></FONT></FONT> Speak no evil about <I>my</I> Vulcan!!!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I loved it Scott Bakula seemed a good fit in his role, and I thought they've done a great job of making it look older that the other series, grittier and with an interesting edge. It's a definite watch for me.<P>And now back to my daydreaming about Jolene Blalock. I wonder if she likes Fieros...     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> *sigh* <P><p>[This message has been edited by Tonker (edited 09-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||09-26-2001||11:20 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B>could've done without the Vulcan Seven-of-9 rip-off</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, she's less of a Seven rip off than the required T&A for Trek.  They've all had the babe quotient (Rand, Troi, Dax, Seven...)- gotta keep the ratings up there.  And she's definately a hottie.<P>I think they did a good job, so far.  But for the love of GOD, I wish Brannon Braga, Ronald Moore, and Rick Berman would stop using TIME TRAVEL at the drop of a hat.  Geez.  It might as well be Quantum Leap with Scott Bakula and the "Temporal Cold War."  I like the concept, and it's visually appealing, but I don't think the people behind the scenes are creative enough - storywise - to keep it interesting and fresh.  I hope they prove me wrong.  I like what I've seen so far.<p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 09-26-2001).]||||reg||1
