Z||000015||Fformula88||09-27-2001||10:15 AM||||After the voyager finale I was worried, but I enjoyed it!  I do agree that the time travel bit is something that they are very fond of, but I don't mind that.  It is science fiction after all!<P>Did anybody notice when Archer goes to "recruit" the linguistic specialist... the word they were trying to pronounce sounded a lot like "Kirk".  Some subliminal messages maybe?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000016||Ken Wittlief||09-27-2001||01:17 PM||||whats up with the networks?!<P>nobody wanted to touch this one - has startrek gotten that low?<P>its on UPN here for crying out loud - a UHF station that broadcasts at about 45W - Even with my antenna on a rotor on the roof it was still fuzzy, and I live in a suburb 10 miles from the transmitter.<P>and its not on any of the sat channels on dish network- unless you want to pay extra for one of the superstations.<P>the only thing in the plot I didnt like was the idea of the Vulcans 'stopping' us from building a warp drive star ship for 100 years?!<P> what was that all about? where are the other planets in the 'federation'? if first contact was already made, then why do the vulcans end up being our wet nurse?!<P> and since zepperan invented the warp drive - how can the vulcans pull rank on us and not allow us to use it for 100 years<P> sounds like some warped version of the prime directive gone sour - since when is one world allowed to hold another one back from progressing?!<P> the show has promise - I was disapointed with the lack of imagination used to come up with the first enterprise - and everything seemed dark in the film exposure department - dont they have floresenct lamps in the 22nd century?<P> hey were talking about a star trek episode on an internet message board - are we all card carrying geeks and nerds or what?!||||reg||1
