Z||000021||Patrick's Dad||09-27-2001||10:27 PM||||I think Enterprise is what Star Trek needs. Actually, I was hoping for Capt. April, when the NCC-1701 was first commisioned....<P>One of the reasons TNG was "almost as good," and the other series seemed to wane in "Trekness" was that the thrill wasn't there. Space flight is old hat. In the new series, it "takes us back" to when interstellar flight is not so common.<P>Bakula was OK. Not a love it or hate it type of casting decision. Blalock wasn't bad. Showed more skin in the first couple of hours than Jeri Ryan did in the entire series. We'll see if she can raise an eyebrow to Nimoy. Most others were somewhat forgettable, although you've got to establish the main relationship on the ship early on. Takei, Nicholls, and Koenig didn't get much of a shakeout early on, either.<P>Troi, eye candy? If so, it's news to me. Props to Ms. Sirtis, she's actually gotten better as she's gotten older (and way more familiar with the character). Even bathing with Riker was a bit lightweight. Dr. Crusher, on the other hand, she was a babe. I have a thing for redheads, and Gates McFadden was a nice weekly fix. Though Diana Muldar was a Trek alum, I was happy to see Gates come back. Dr. Polanski was supposed to be the second coming of Dr. McCoy, but Dr. Crusher just fit better in the show.<P>Anyway, I'll be watching Enterprise, and waiting for the answers to:<P>1) Who are the Suliban, and how did they get destroyed (They have never been mentioned in any Trek, and they're close by)?<P>2) Why isn't there a picture of NX-01 in the NCC-1701 "Gallery of Enterprises?" See ST-TMP. V'Ger's probe in Ilia's body states that carbon based units have "stunted the growth" of Enterprise.<P>3) What will the Tholians/Gorn/Orion Pirates/etc. look like now that there's a substantial makeup budget?<P>Lastly, I don't mind the time travel stuff so much, as long as it isn't overdone. In fact, I already knew that you were going to complain about it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000022||87FieroGTx||09-28-2001||03:47 AM|||| I loved everything but the THEME SONG it hasto go!||||reg||1
Z||000023||Formula88||09-28-2001||09:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>the only thing in the plot I didnt like was the idea of the Vulcans 'stopping' us from building a warp drive star ship for 100 years?!<P> what was that all about? where are the other planets in the 'federation'? if first contact was already made, then why do the vulcans end up being our wet nurse?!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, here's the way I see it, Cochran's Warp engine was probably only good for Warp 1, barely.  Even at that speed, it's still impractical to make interstellar flights.  Interplanetary, sure, but not interstellar.  So the Warp 5 engine project would be necessary to make interstellar flights useful.  I saw the Vulcans has trying to help us as much as they could, but without giving us technology.  It could have taken us 100+ years easily to go from Warp 1 to Warp 5, just depends on how fast our development worked.  Remember, we went from the 1st space flight to the first moon landing in less than 20 years, but in the 30 years since then, we still haven't gotten farther than the moon.  We most likely spent that 100 years in low warp ships knocking around our own solar system.  <P>Also, the Federation probably doesn't exist yet.  I don't know when it was founded, but I believe it was founded by Earth, and that would be pretty silly at their level of development.  Who'd join up?  That would be like Ethiopia starting a Global Space Program and asking the US to join.||||reg||6
Z||000024||btoth||09-28-2001||09:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87FieroGTx:<BR><B> I loved everything but the THEME SONG it hasto go!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes!  That was my first and only <I>real</I> complaint... the theme song reminded me of Baywatch (don't know why).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I liked the theme song for Voyager.  Maybe the begining will change as the season goes on... then they'll have more stuff to show durring the credits.||||reg||1
Z||000025||LZeitgeist||09-28-2001||09:48 AM||||I liked it. The imagery behind the opening theme was *perfect*, and I even liked the theme...<P>It's a new take on things, and it's got incredible potential... my only preference is that they do *not* screw up established continuity. However, they seem to already have those bases covered by not just having a single 'time travel' episode to fix whatever harm they do at the end of the series, but they have a continuous 'time alteration' theme going on here... as long as they don't use it as a crutch, it might turn out to be interesting...<P>I also have to vote for more gratuitous 'refrigerated decon' scenes, as long as T'Pol is a standard member of the Away Teams...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I mean, dayam... <P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000026||Ken Wittlief||09-28-2001||11:33 AM||||That would have been a great line in the decom chamber "Is it chilly in here or are you just glad to see me?"  :c)||||reg||10
Z||000027||Tonker||09-28-2001||12:53 PM||||At first I didn't like the theme song either, but then I realized it fits in really well. It's something different, a little less futuristic, and it doesn't really hint at "Star Trek", because that universe as we know it, doesn't exist yet.||||reg||14
