Z||000040||Ken Wittlief||10-03-2001||09:56 AM||||the show is running the risk of following the same old formulas.<BR> <BR> the felix character, now the doctor<P> does every starship have to have a vulcan for a science officer?!<P>  the perky babe crewmember<P>did you know the plots of most of the original star trek episodes were bsaed on cowboy (ie bonanza) script formulas.<P> thats why in almost every early episode there was a fist fight - it was a wild west cowboy story set in outer space.<P> BTW have you noticed lately - if you watch the original series now, on your state of the art color tv, or better yet, from a sattelite, that when they have a fight seen you can CLEARLY tell when the stunt doubles are on screen?<P> back when ST first aired the clarity and resoultion of TV sets, esp color tv sets, was poor - but now the stunt doubles are very obvious - so obvious that its funny.<P> hey they showed the pilot of TNG the other day - the farpoint mission - and it had a SERIOUS error in it.<P> near the beginning they separate the saucer section from the rest of the ship, at warp 9.4!<P> so now the saucer section is, is what?! coasting through space at warp 9.4?! with no warp nacells present?!<P>  isnt warp speed achieved because the warp nacells bend space?! so if the saucer is separated and the 'battle configuration' part of the ship turns around and goes the other way, then what happens to the saucers section when it is no longer in the 'bent space' - I think it would splatter into dust.<P> or if it was left coasting at warp 9.4, how in the h#ll is it going to stop with no warp engines?!<P>  oops!<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000041||DaRkLoRD||10-03-2001||12:31 PM||||hehe.. star trek is full of those things.. in fact there are books written about all the inconsistancies in the episodes, one of the ones I rememeber reading (I didn't buy the book..) was in the pilot for ST: TNG, the computer tells Riker to turn right down a hall to get to the holodeck, and he turns left.. heh.. (or the other way around)<BR>I've also seen some shots where the same button does several different things, within the same scene.. eg. one button fires the phasers, then the next second without changing anything, the same button fires the photon torpedos.. oh well, there are mistakes in every tv show!<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
Z||000042||Ken Wittlief||10-03-2001||11:17 PM||||its not which button you push, its HOW you push it that matters.<P> my favorite running joke on ST, esp TNG, is everytime they need a technological miracle, its time for a field of tachyon particles.<P> I swear, in every other episode they are doing some new wonderfull thing with tachyon particles.<P>  Must be the starship equivalent of catsup. Use it on everything.||||reg||10
